{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1385669-fixing-slivers-for-c20","id":1385669,"title":"Fixing Slivers for C20","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-04T15:51:10-07:00","id":1385669,"title":"Fixing Slivers for C20","content":"So before I work on new inanimae stuff I need to fix Slivers. But how? Should I keep the Inanimae Realms or just give them the normal realm spread. How much should I diverge from the original slivers?<br /> <br /> <br /> And here are the Sliver Ideas SLIVER IDEAS:<br /> <br /> Flux for Pyros, since they mention fire wroughts change.<br /> <br /> Stasis/Morphus for Petros as the Earth is about form and permanence.<br /> <br /> Ktisis/Dimiourgia/Chaos for Verdage, basically the Creation birth aspect of plantlife.<br /> <br /> Aionios for Aquas, since the splinters associated water with time just make a splinter about time and eternity.<br /> <br /> Apeiron for Stratus since the Splinters associated air with space, have a splinter dedicated just to space/indefinition/chaos.<br /> <br /> Others:<br /> <br /> Osseus for the missing element of Bone, for the Homonculus Inanimae, perhaps as suggested it represents a primordial precursor to the Mannikins as an aspect of spirit.<br /> <br /> Thanatos could be the subtle variant of Osseus, representing Death and even the other worlds of the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Datum could be a new Sliver from those born of the nascent Empire of the Machine. It could represent purpose and Knowledge like those from a purposely created machine, the manipulations of simple machines, and even recorded data.<br /> <br /> Logos could be the subtle Sliver for Datum, representing Order, Intent, Reason, and consciousness.<br /> <br /> Splinters of the Heart Question<br /> <br /> Maybe for the Heart question we could also include some secret Slivers Inanimae seek to master. Maybe the Heart question could represent the Inanimae's version of the Siochain.<br /> <br /> Eros being the heart of the heart question. Love, especially as known by humanity is a divine secret the Inanimae often would give quite a lot to find out. Thus their version of Golconda could have a sliver harnessing it, which naturally also includes Anteros, hate. But this isn't the blunt art that was <br /> <br /> Aphrodisios that got converted and cannibalized into Summer. This would also represent want, and possibly even hope.<br /> <br /> Gnosis would be the splinter that could possibly represent the missing piece of the divine, and purpose that the heart question could fulfil.<br /> <br /> Agon would be the Splinter known well to the mortal heart, perhaps even more then Eros. Suffering is something rocks may not be naturally familiar with but to seek the Heart Question you must learn the suffering of a man's heart.<br /> <br /> Deimos and finally the splinter representing dread. Like the other three Heart Question Splinters, dread and loss are not something Elemental beings were necessarily born with, but it cuts at the heart of the issue. To know man is to know the potential for loss. For Fear. Pinnochio may never have found the blue faery at the end if he did not truly have it in him to fear loss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T16:55:00-07:00","id":1385681,"title":"","content":"So, One thing that Iv'e thought about was actually using the unleash rule. But with a few modifications.<br /> <br /> First, inanimae spend less glamour to unleash(only 1 point), and no glamour to unleash from the element they are connected with. <br /> <br /> <br /> Second, give off a few conceptual powers that each element has. Eg<br /> <br /> Aquis: purify, cure, see far away/past/future, make it rain/snow, use water to attack, etc. (Probably many more could be listed)<br /> <br /> Whenever a inanimae buy a realm(they will need realms), they can choose one of the effects listed, and get a automatic sucess whenever they unleash trying for such effect (with any realm). This makes unleashing results be more predictable, but since the list of effects can be so big (not to mention others slivers) it also means the inanimae will probably be specialized on certains effects. <br /> <br /> Of course, effects outside of the listed can still be used, as long as the player justify how the concept ties with the choosen element","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T18:03:01-07:00","id":1385697,"title":"","content":"Interesting you are the first I have seen who would prefer to keep the only unleashing choice!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T18:29:07-07:00","id":1385701,"title":"","content":"Well, the problem with Unleashing Only is that it's expensive and wild; if there was a way to tone down those aspects of it, to let Slivers do with Unleashing what Arts do with their Cantrips, it would be less of a problem. <br /> <br /> I rather like the inversion of Realms in this notion: rather than Realms building up on what Cantrips can do, They could be used here to restrain what a Sliver's Unleashing does: using a Sliver without the use of Realms is just like Unleashing an Art; but as you apply Realms to the effect, you harness the wildness of it (in a manner determined by the Realms used) and get something more Cantrip-like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T19:27:09-07:00","id":1385715,"title":"","content":"I think we do need more then just one sliver for each element. That is why my proposed model is each element has a phenomenal Sliver and a subtle silver and 4 Heart Slivers. This makes a much more robust variety of powers for my liking.<br /> <br /> But in Dark Age Fae the Inanimae were actually the ones who specialized in Weaving, having been the ones to teach Humanity weaving in the form of mastering fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T19:58:35-07:00","id":1385720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1385669-fixing-slivers-for-c20?p=1385715#post1385715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we do need more then just one sliver for each element. That is why my proposed model is each element has a phenomenal Sliver and a subtle silver and 4 Heart Slivers. This makes a much more robust variety of powers for my liking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, now your original post makes sense. (Bear in mind that if you laid out the groundwork for this elsewhere, I probably haven't seen it.)<br /> <br /> With that in mind: <br /> <br /> The Promethean fan in me giggles when you say that Pyros is paired with Flux; and I'm okay with that. <br /> <br /> I'd pair Petros with Stasis and Verdage with Ktisis. I also like the association of Water and Air with Time and Space. <br /> <br /> Instead of Heart Slivers, have you considered adapting the Graces from Exalted: Fair Folk/Graceful Wicked Masques? Or were you thinking of making that a modern Firstborn thing? (Possibly an alternative to Arts and Realms for the Dark-kin?)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1385669-fixing-slivers-for-c20?p=1385715#post1385715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But in Dark Age Fae the Inanimae were actually the ones who specialized in Weaving, having been the ones to teach Humanity weaving in the form of mastering fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Dark Ages: Fae, <i>everyone</i> could both Weave and Unleash; and the Inanimae were in fact the most balanced of the three Origins in this regard (Changelings had a bias toward Weaving, and the Firstborn had a bias toward the Mists, a.k.a. Unleashing). In the Sundering, a lot was lost: Changelings migrated even more heavily toward Weaving, leading to the modern Arts; and the Firstborn retreated to Arcadia, never to return (unless you consider the Dark Kin to be the returned Firstborn). I could see the Inanimae suffering a similar restriction, in their case losing the Cantrips that come with Weaving and having to rely more heavily on Unleashing as a result.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-04-2020, 11:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T20:35:17-07:00","id":1385727,"title":"","content":"Yeah sorry I was copy and pasting notes from my phone when I posted this. I realized I didn't explain how I think each Element should have two representative Slivers.<br /> A lot of people were fans of the Graces, myself included. I came up with the Heart Slivers because of the barely talked about Riddle of the Heart in Inanimae Secret Ways. So I just took what I think would be alien to folks like Pinocchio or a sentient rock but that would be intrinsic and inseparable from the human condition. Things deeply tied to spirituality so Love, Suffering, Fear, and spiritual wisdom all wrapped up in the riddle of the heart which probably would be something like Want.<br /> <br /> Good point about the Dark Ages, the Inanimae weren't the best weavers they were just the ones to first teach humanity.<br /> <br /> I figured after I figure out how Slivers work then I can make more Phyla like the Homunculi, and in-between things like Gargoyles. <br /> <br /> <br /> But limiting Inanimae to only Unleashings was purely motivated by lack of word count, originally the Inanimae had Slivers and their own special version of realms defined by the elements.<br /> <br /> I think there is oodles of potential with the Inanimae but nobody does anything with them because nobody wants to play them when you can play a changeling with actually defined powers.<br /> <br /> My idea is both Inanimae and Changeling can develop Dominions if they meet certain prerequisites. As Slivers are called Slivers because they are supposed to represent just a sliver of the power of the True Fae before the coming of Banality (I too keep confusing the Shattering with the Sundering). Then when they made Dark Age Fae they made Dominions, which are powerful but a little to simple, making it kind of omnipotent.<br /> <br /> And it just seemed perfect to pair Pyros and Flux, especially with the associations of Fire in Inanimae the Secret Ways. They were the Inanimae that brought change to the universe.<br /> <br /> <br /> What if Inanimae can learn specifically the Seasonal Arts?<br /> <br /> <br /> Here are my ideas on Arts and Splinters converging in their Greater Arts/Sliver the Dominions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#1C1E21\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">So the idea is these Greater Arts require prerequisites, which are flexible prerequisites but represent certain competence to tap into primordial thematic power. So I'm thinking a lot of them require mastery of at least one of the Associated Arts, or maybe they need mastery of a specific Seasonal Art along with others. Maybe knowing a dot in certain arts counts as a certain amount of points while Seasonal arts twice the points. The idea being Seasonal are maybe the most primordial and old of the Fae Magic. Meanwhile lets say Inanimae can learn these as well, but they usually learn it through Splinters. And like splinters they have a permanent buff, but can also used with realms for cantrips and can be Unleashed. Maybe for Changelings/Inanimae/Dark-kin they need to like Glamour 6 to tap into it. Mean True Fae can learn it off the bat without learning other Arts.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#1C1E21\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Greater Art of Mistweaving</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#1C1E21\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Conjuring potential from the Mists, pure master of Glamour, and possibly even the birth of Fae from the Primordial Mists. Its the mastery of the Unknown, Dreaming and Mystery. This is the Art the First Fae used to create the Mists that dull the memories of Changelings and Mortal alike. Prerequisites 13 dots from either Naming, Chicanery, Primal, Oneiromancy, Seasonal Arts (at least 2 Dots of Seasonal Arts) and if new arts are created Talecraft.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#1C1E21\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Greater Art of Dawn</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#1C1E21\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The art of beginnings, past, birth, potential, hope, and spring. This Art carved the first dawn from the Endless Night. Prerequisite 13 dots in either Spring, Pyretics, Naming, Primal, Metamorphosis, Chronos, and Soothsay.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#1C1E21\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Greater Art of Day</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#1C1E21\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The art of life, existence, light, warmth, faith, clarity and summer. This art brought forth being from nonbeing. Prerequisite 13 dots in Summer, Pyretics, Naming, Primal, and Sovereign.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#1C1E21\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Greater Art of Dusk</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#1C1E21\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The art of endings, dimming, entropy, fatalism, time and autumn. This art brought passing and change to the world. Prerequisite 13 dots in Autumn, Naming, Primal, Metamorphosis, Chronos, Soothsay, and Wayfare.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#1C1E21\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Greater Art of Night</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#1C1E21\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The art of death, naught, darkness, cold, nihilism, sleep and Winter. This art was the first and final night existing before time and Creation. Prerequisite 13 dots in Winter, Naming, Primal, Skycraft, Autumn, Ruin, and Spirit-Link/whatever death art gets made.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#1C1E21\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Greater Art of the Deep</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#1C1E21\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The art of primordial depths, infinity, eternity, the sea, and below. This was the art of the endless sea from which everything sprang. Prerequisite 13 dots in Primal, Naming, Skycraft, and Oneiromancy. Whatever ocean or underground art are developed. The Fomorians mastered this, as did Vatea of the Mer and from which Turtle Island sprang.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#1C1E21\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Greater Art of Nightmare</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#1C1E21\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The art of Fear, primordial darkness, instinct, wilderness, madness, and Nightmares. This was the Art mastered by the Fomorian Hosts in the Darkest Corners of the Dreaming. Prerequisite 13 dots in Primal, Naming Oneiromancy, Autumn, and Skycraft.</span></span></span></div><br /> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#1C1E21\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'm thinking this would be more expensive than other arts, maybe the first dot particularly expensive, maybe costing 25 dots for the first Dot, and rating times 6 to increase?</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#1C1E21\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Maybe part of the basic effects of the first foundation dot in a Greater Art kind of makes you less mortal.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T22:49:17-07:00","id":1386012,"title":"","content":"My plan Patch and expand Inanimae for use is first to redo their Splinter. Then introduce Homunculus Phyla who are made from corpses. Then explore the idea of alternate Phyla for the Elements, because the original Inanimae the Secret Ways seems to express that there are many more phyla but the ones given are just examples using the most common of each Element. For instance I would make a Nymph variant for each Element, as Nymphs seem to be the natural inspiration for inanimae.<br /> <br /> And I plan to flesh out the Heart Question as the Inanimae version of Golconda/Siobhan. <br /> <br /> Then after I touch upon some kiths I want to flesh out I will work on the idea of Dominion powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T04:39:36-07:00","id":1386949,"title":"","content":"Here are my ideas for the Sliver Advantages (those free powers you get when you learn the first dot of a Sliver) for the Subtle Slivers. It seems to me the intent when they designed the Inanimae was that they very much concentrated on their elements associated Sliver, with it being significant for each time dipping into other Slivers since they only originally had five. With the option of providing more Slivers I still keep this in mind, but now each Element has two slivers. Though not to the Degree that Inanimae were specialized, older editions of Changeling seemed to go with the idea the vast majority of Fae only had a handful of Arts, as fae were numerous and not known for each individual being broadly magically powerful, and those who were were called sorcerers. In fact I got the Impression most Fae probably didn't learn more then 5 different levels of arts in their lifetime, hence why folks with jobs as Knights or Guards weren't broad sources of many magical tricks, their skill defined them more then their Magic it seemed.<br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#1d2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Flux</b> for Pyros, since they mention fire wroughts change.</span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#1d2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Gift learned with the first dot of Flux is the capacity to altern emotions of those touched. Roll Manipulation and Flux and you can trigger an emotional streak in the calm, or stear one emotion to a different emotion.</span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#1d2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Opposed Sliver: Stasis</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> </div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#1d2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Stasis/Morphus</b> for Petros as the Earth is about form and permanence.</span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#1d2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stasis when learned allows the Inanimae to sleep without Nourishment or Air for as long as they wish. They may also roll Stasis and Stamina to make a sleeping individual not awaken unless attacked for the Scene, as well as sleep an extra hour for each success. If suffering from Poison or Disease a hibernating individual will suspend suffering injury while slumbering.</span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#1d2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Opposed Sliver: Flux (I might actually make Two Subtle Slivers for Petros as I think Morphus and Stasis have enough room to be two fully fleshed out Slivers.)</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> </div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#1d2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Ktisis/Dimiourgia/Chaos</b> for Verdage, basically the Creation birth aspect of plantlife.</span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#1d2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ktisis instils the gift of life to the Inanimae allowing them to cause seeds to immediately sprout, and eggs to hatch even if unfertilized (Parthenogenesis). They may even coach a tree into bearing fruit, roll Kitises and Charisma with each success creating enough food for one meal, or to hatch a single egg or seed (miniscule seeds like grass would be a patch of grass per success). It can also cause seeds or growth from already dead plantlife.</span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#1d2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Opposed Sliver: Stasis</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> </div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#1d2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Aionios</b> for Aquas, since the splinters associated water with time just make a splinter about time and eternity.</span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#1d2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Aionios gives those who learn it a perfect reckoning of time, understanding the date down to the millisecond, as well as setting perfect alarm clocks or stopwatches. Roll Aionios + Perception to notice temporal manipulation.</span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#1d2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Opposed Sliver: Apeiron</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> </div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#1d2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Apeiron</b> for Stratus since the Splinters associated air with space, have a splinter dedicated just to space/indefinition/chaos.</span></span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#1d2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Apeiron students have a perfected spatial awareness, able to tell how big a room is, or how much volume of water a tub contains, and even count how many jelly beans in a jar at a fair. Roll Apeiron + Perception to triangulate spatial disturbances such as portals or teleportation.</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> </div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#1d2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Opposed Sliver: Aionios</span></span></span></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","user":"Eldagusto","date":".  Spacing and Bolding 05-09-2020, 07:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T06:02:51-07:00","id":1386964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1385669-fixing-slivers-for-c20?p=1385697#post1385697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting you are the first I have seen who would prefer to keep the only unleashing choice!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Actually I don't really prefer that way, but If im not going to use it, then I would probably use the older system. But so far, the ideas floating here looked intereting and Im actually thinking inanimaes as a whole could be reworked/retconned from the ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T08:52:43-07:00","id":1386980,"title":"","content":"If you bring in Osseus and Thanatos, then I'd recommend pairing Verdage and Osseus as opposed Slivers, and Ktisis and Thanatos as opposed Slivers, rather than Ktisis being opposed by Stasis. Alternately, if you treat Stasis and Morphus as separate Slivers, then I'd choose one of them to oppose Flux (probably Stasis) and the other to oppose Ktisis (by extension, Morphus).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T12:46:08-07:00","id":1387049,"title":"","content":"Those are good suggestions. I was thinking of Ktisis and Thanatos for interest being opposed but I was wondering if rarer Slivers should be linked to main ones. But you are right. If I am redoing things from scratch why not if it makes the most sense!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T13:27:05-07:00","id":1387061,"title":"","content":"Osseus for the missing element of Bone, for the Homonculus Inanimae, perhaps as suggested it represents a primordial precursor to the Mannikins as an aspect of spirit.<br /> <br /> Osseus teaches one to sniff out the dead. Roll Osseus and Perception to sense corpses if hidden from view, or notice if ghosts are present.<br /> <br /> Opposed Sliver: Verdage <br /> <br /> Thanatos could be the subtle variant of Osseus, representing Death and even the other worlds of the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Thanatos brings the capacity to bring calm painless death with a Thanatos + Charisma roll to those who seek and end to their suffering or for small animals with two or less Health levels remaining or those less then half the size of the inanimae with a resisted roll. It can also help fight disease and Cancer with a Thanatos + Dexterity roll acting similar to acute Chemo, adding successes to their stamina rolls to fight the illness.<br /> Opposed Sliver: Ktisis<br /> <br /> <br /> Datum could be a new Sliver from those born of the nascent Empire of the Machine. It could represent purpose and Knowledge like those from a purposely created machine, the manipulations of simple machines, and even recorded data.<br /> <br /> Datum allows one to read from any device one touches whether as simple as a book or as complex as a computer. Rolling Datum + Wits allows one to tap into wifi and other invisible signals for one stolen snippet of phone conversation or television.<br /> Opposed Sliver is Pyros<br /> <br /> Logos could be the subtle Sliver for Datum, representing Order, Intent, Reason, and consciousness.<br /> <br /> Those with intimate experience with Logos may Roll Logos and Charisma to have a spoken or written single phrase understood, even plants and animals will understand the mean to some extend even if limited in how to react.<br /> Opposed Sliver is Flux<br /> <br /> <br /> I\u2019m also thinking I will have combination Sliver Powers called Alchemies.<br /> <br /> I may just have the Inanimae use the basic realms or I may give them their original 4 Elements plus Spirit as their realms as original found in their book.<br /> <br /> I may make a Morphus Sliver for Earth and an Asma Sliver for Air as the music Sliver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T16:28:55-07:00","id":1387118,"title":"","content":"I am thinking seasonal arts I will allow the Inanimae to learn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T19:26:09-07:00","id":1387395,"title":"","content":"I had a quick look over 2nd ed Inanimae, Unleashing, and DA: Fae for reference and am spitballing an alternate idea that may potentially worth testing out:<br /> <br /> Tweak the Hsein rules for Elemental Alchemy, but substituting &quot;wind&quot; for metal, altering the casting style to be based off Sliver+Inanimae Realms instead of Fortune dice, and replacing &quot;yin/yang&quot; with &quot;season&quot;. Similar to how in DA: Fae, you had Common Cantrips that worked differently based off which domain you were casting from, you can modify the base &quot;elemental alchemy&quot; effects based off which Season is being used. <br /> <br /> It's late so I may explore this more later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25625-magicjuggler","name":"MagicJuggler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25625_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T06:03:04-07:00","id":1387465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagicJuggler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1385669-fixing-slivers-for-c20?p=1387395#post1387395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a quick look over 2nd ed Inanimae, Unleashing, and DA: Fae for reference and am spitballing an alternate idea that may potentially worth testing out:<br /> <br /> Tweak the Hsein rules for Elemental Alchemy, but substituting &quot;wind&quot; for metal, altering the casting style to be based off Sliver+Inanimae Realms instead of Fortune dice, and replacing &quot;yin/yang&quot; with &quot;season&quot;. Similar to how in DA: Fae, you had Common Cantrips that worked differently based off which domain you were casting from, you can modify the base &quot;elemental alchemy&quot; effects based off which Season is being used.<br /> <br /> It's late so I may explore this more later.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an interesting idea, my nature was to have Inanimae also exist in Asia but maybe in smaller numbers, as lost to history a great deal of their Numbers became the Nobles of the Fae who served Heaven. But you could even just add Wind rather then replace Metal, hell that is an interesting idea for Hsien use as well. The Season Approach though is particularly inspired, while I initially passed over the idea when I first read about how Inanimae Worked (I read Land of Eight Million Dreams first), but using the Seasons is an approach that makes it all of a sudden more appealing. Any reason to convince me to work on more Hsien Material. :P<br /> <br /> But more and more it feels like the Seasonal Arts, being the most Primeval of the Arts, should be Available to the Inanimae, like a powerset that bridges the divide between Kithain and Inanimae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T03:34:31-07:00","id":1387677,"title":"","content":"While I'm still deciding the nature of how they will use Realms I do like the simplicity and elegance of Materiel replacing Bunks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T12:06:02-07:00","id":1387771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1385669-fixing-slivers-for-c20?p=1387465#post1387465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is an interesting idea, my nature was to have Inanimae also exist in Asia but maybe in smaller numbers, as lost to history a great deal of their Numbers became the Nobles of the Fae who served Heaven. But you could even just add Wind rather then replace Metal, hell that is an interesting idea for Hsien use as well. The Season Approach though is particularly inspired, while I initially passed over the idea when I first read about how Inanimae Worked (I read Land of Eight Million Dreams first), but using the Seasons is an approach that makes it all of a sudden more appealing. Any reason to convince me to work on more Hsien Material. :P<br /> <br /> But more and more it feels like the Seasonal Arts, being the most Primeval of the Arts, should be Available to the Inanimae, like a powerset that bridges the divide between Kithain and Inanimae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Primal would be the most primeval of the Arts, actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T01:44:58-07:00","id":1388269,"title":"","content":"So what are peoples thoughts on the original Inanimae Realms of the Four Elements plus Spirit replacing Fae? Walking away from Arcadia did an interesting take updating them but also adding Carnalis for Meat, can't seem to find that article anymore though.<br /> <br /> Is the Element themes worth ditching the wonderfully fleshed out basic Realm system? I'm leaning more towards Normal realms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T06:03:39-07:00","id":1388309,"title":"","content":"I'd go with normal Realms, too: the Elemental-themed ones take the Elemental theming of literally everything a step too far. If you want to retain anything from there, just introduce alternate names for the existing Realms (e.g., \u201cthe Inanimae sometimes refer to Fae as Spirit\u201d); but mechanically, don't change anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T20:16:37-07:00","id":1393314,"title":"","content":"After I finish reading the players guide fully I plan to try to work on one of my vault projects fully and more and more I\u2019m thinking about either Inanimae revising the Slivers or Psychic the Discovery. Or a smaller project first. And I am still learning pdf crafting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T20:30:35-07:00","id":1393319,"title":"","content":"If you have access to Word on a laptop or desktop (not a mobile device), you can use one of the Word Templates from Storyteller's Vault to do all of the formatting for you and just use a PDF converter to turn it into a pdf when you're done. The main thing that's been stalling me out is that I pretty much have to do everything on mobile devices these days; and the mobile version of Word doesn't let you install custom templates (I'd kill for a way to install custom templates on an iPad). Heck, you have to jump through some hoops just to install the fonts; but that at least is doable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T20:41:29-07:00","id":1393324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1385669-fixing-slivers-for-c20?p=1393319#post1393319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have access to Word on a laptop or desktop (not a mobile device), you can use one of the Word Templates from Storyteller's Vault to do all of the formatting for you and just use a PDF converter to turn it into a pdf when you're done. The main thing that's been stalling me out is that I pretty much have to do everything on mobile devices these days; and the mobile version of Word doesn't let you install custom templates (I'd kill for a way to install custom templates on an iPad). Heck, you have to jump through some hoops just to install the fonts; but that at least is doable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know the pain. I\u2019ve never tried different templates before but I downloaded the pdf packs, man they were big. I have long time ago used Custom fonts but that is it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T20:44:57-07:00","id":1393327,"title":"","content":"Find the section in the downloads about Word Templates, and look up what's involved in installing a custom templates in Word. Once you've done so, create a new file based on that template and start writing. Word should take care of most or all of the formatting for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T02:34:34-07:00","id":1404557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1385669-fixing-slivers-for-c20?p=1393327#post1393327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Find the section in the downloads about Word Templates, and look up what's involved in installing a custom templates in Word. Once you've done so, create a new file based on that template and start writing. Word should take care of most or all of the formatting for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I spent the whole night trying to see if I can edit the PDF templates without buying a Word subscription, and I downloaded free Word Processors and the like, but it all seems very much designed to have you pay for a subscription somewhere in order to shift all these around oiii.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar